            <ArticleTitle>[The mechanisms of the participation of the peptidergic systems in regulating respiratory center function].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In experiments on different species of animals respiratory stimulating effects of naloxone, TRH and its analogue RGH 2202 during respiratory rhythmogenesis disturbances, evoked by hyperventilation of lungs, bleeding and intoxication with cyanides or opiates, were investigated. The role of opiate and NMDA receptors in respiratory centre function is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
